/*!
 * \addtogroup in-out-delimin
 *
 * \brief Delimitation of input streams
 *
 * An essential feature of data transmission using BER/DER is that the tags that compose it can--and
 * in fact usually do--have a definite length (see ber::tag_header::length). The library natively
 * implements a wrapper that abstracts the decoders from the availability of octets in a
 * ber::octet_input based on the tag length.
 *
 * \note **Rationale**:
 * It doesn't make sense to delegate the implementation of this feature to the library client every
 * time.
 *
 * Only implementations of ber::delimited_input::skippable can be wrapped by an input delimiter.
 * Input stream implementations should take this into account to adhere to this native feature.
 */

